    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "PATZ1-rearranged sarcoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "PATZ1-rearranged sarcoma from the back of a 54-year-old male. This example is surrounded by a fibrous capsule associated with lymphoid aggregates. There is an equal mixture of relatively bland glomoid and spindle cells set in a fibromyxoid matrix. A characteristic arborizing vascular network of thin-walled hyalinized vessels is present. This tumor also shows intratumoral lymphoid aggregates and small foci of mature-appearing adipose tissue.",
    "source": "Jorge Torres-Mora",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/55133.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 79988,
    "bookid": 87,
    "chapterId": 288,
    "fileId": 55189,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "PATZ1-rearranged sarcoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<span data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Sarcoma with an EWSR1:: PATZ1 gene fusion arising&nbsp; in the neck of a 27-year-old male surrounded by an irregular fibrous capsule with tumor protrusions. The tumor is composed of round to plump spindle cells arranged in vaguely fascicular, whorling&nbsp; and&nbsp; reticular patterns. The stroma is fibromyxoid and multiple microcysts of variable size and shape filled with proteinaceous material are scattered throughout the tumor.</span>",
    "source": "Jorge Torres-Mora",
    "copyright": "",
